BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 5120 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: SCIN010067892026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice Sanjiv Khanna & Justice B.V. Nagarathna

PARTIES:
Internet Freedom Foundation
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Union of India, Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023, Consumer Protection Act 2019, Constitution of India

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
DPDP Act Section 6, Article 21, Consumer Protection Act Section 2\(9\)

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Dark Patterns, Digital Privacy, Informed Consent, Data Autonomy, K.S. Puttaswamy

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Challenge to pre-checked cookie consents and deceptive subscription interfaces on government and commercial portals.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Do dark patterns that nudge users into involuntarily relinquishing personal data breach the constitutional right to privacy?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Consent procured through dark patterns or UI deception is null and void ab initio; true digital consent must be freely given, specific, and unambiguous.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Civil Appeal Allowed; Automated dark patterns and deceptive consent mechanisms declared violative of digital privacy.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice Sanjiv Khanna & Justice B.V. Nagarathna
Supreme Court of India
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
